args: opentide query --help
exit: 0

━━━ stdout
Run a read-only query on platform tenants and show rows

Sends the query, or a rule's query, to each selected tenant over the
window and prints at most --limit rows per tenant. No search or rule is
saved on the tenant.

␛[1m␛[4mUsage:␛[0m ␛[1mopentide query␛[0m [OPTIONS] ␛[1m--platform␛[0m <PLATFORM> [query]

␛[1m␛[4mArguments:␛[0m
  [query]
          The query, in the platform's language. '-' reads it from stdin

␛[1m␛[4mOptions:␛[0m
      ␛[1m--platform␛[0m <PLATFORM>
          Detection platform: sentinel, defender_for_endpoint, splunk, sentinel_one, crowdstrike, harfanglab, carbon_black_cloud, elastic, sysdig, bitdefender, graylog, exabeam, google_secops
          
          [possible values: sentinel, defender_for_endpoint, splunk, sentinel_one, crowdstrike, harfanglab, carbon_black_cloud, elastic, sysdig, bitdefender, graylog, exabeam, google_secops]

      ␛[1m--tenant␛[0m <TENANT>
          Run on this tenant (repeatable), or 'all'. Default: the only tenant configured

      ␛[1m--rule␛[0m <RULE>
          Run the query this rule (by UUID) deploys to the platform

      ␛[1m--file␛[0m <FILE>
          Run the query of the rule in this file

      ␛[1m--query-file␛[0m <QUERY_FILE>
          Read the query from this file

      ␛[1m--since␛[0m <SINCE>
          Look back this far from --to or now: 15m, 24h, 7d, PT1H. Default: 24h

      ␛[1m--from␛[0m <START>
          Start of the window, ISO-8601 (UTC unless it names an offset)

      ␛[1m--to␛[0m <END>
          End of the window, ISO-8601. Default: now

      ␛[1m--limit␛[0m <LIMIT>
          Rows per tenant, at most 5000
          
          [default: 100]

      ␛[1m--language␛[0m <LANGUAGE>
          Elastic only: esql (default), eql, lucene or kuery

      ␛[1m--index␛[0m <INDEX>
          Elastic index pattern, CrowdStrike repository or Graylog stream alias (repeatable)

      ␛[1m--timeout␛[0m <TIMEOUT>
          Seconds to wait for a search to finish
          
          [default: 120.0]

      ␛[1m--columns␛[0m <COLUMNS>
          Comma-separated columns the table shows

      ␛[1m--format␛[0m <ROW_FORMAT>
          table, jsonl or csv (--json prints the envelope)
          
          [default: table]
          [possible values: table, jsonl, csv]

      ␛[1m--help␛[0m
          Print help

Examples:
  $ opentide query --platform sentinel 'SecurityEvent | take 10'
  $ opentide query --platform splunk --rule <rule-uuid> --tenant all --since 7d
  $ opentide query --platform elastic --language eql --index 'logs-*' --format jsonl 'process where process.name == "cmd.exe"'

━━━ stderr · empty
